WEBVTT

00:00:49.150 --> 00:00:51.700
What the hell are they thinking ?! 
This straightaway's too short for that !

00:00:52.150 --> 00:00:54.900
Hey, that's Takahashi Ryosuke's white FC !

00:00:55.300 --> 00:00:56.800
Are they battling ?

00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:10.800
An R32 GT-R.

00:01:14.900 --> 00:01:16.450
He's better than I thought.

00:01:20.100 --> 00:01:23.360
I can keep up with Takahashi Ryosuke.

00:01:31.900 --> 00:01:35.500
Young Magazine 35th Anniversary Production

00:01:37.700 --> 00:01:40.850
As I thought, you're Takahashi
 Ryosuke of the Akagi Red Suns.

00:01:43.530 --> 00:01:44.200
And you ?

00:01:46.300 --> 00:01:49.350
I'm Nakazato Takeshi of the Myogi Night Kids

00:01:49.350 --> 00:01:50.200
Nakazato...

00:01:51.470 --> 00:01:52.900
I've heard your name at least.

00:01:53.550 --> 00:01:57.760
So, what's a Myogi street racer doing in Akina ?

00:01:57.760 --> 00:02:00.700
Look who's talking. 
You're an Akagi street racer.

00:02:00.700 --> 00:02:04.300
Both of us have the same objective.

00:02:07.810 --> 00:02:10.000
I never expected someone like that in Akina.

00:02:11.180 --> 00:02:17.600
A driver of a GT-R tuned to 380 HP
 is planning to challenge Akina's Eight-Six ?

00:02:19.100 --> 00:02:21.900
How did you know the power of my car's engine ?

00:02:22.760 --> 00:02:28.610
The battle will be very one-sided, and the outcome is obvious before you even try.

00:02:29.000 --> 00:02:32.500
{nobori}The GT-R will win hands down on 
the uphill, thanks to its power, but...

00:02:32.500 --> 00:02:36.000
...you can't beat that Eight-Six on the
 downhill, no matter how hard you try.

00:02:36.000 --> 00:02:37.100
Say what ?!

00:02:37.610 --> 00:02:42.000
Don't get me wrong. 
I just spoke my mind.

00:02:43.050 --> 00:02:45.250
Don't screw around with me.

00:02:45.250 --> 00:02:48.400
If you put it that way, 
I can't back off no matter what.

00:02:48.400 --> 00:02:51.520
{ano}I'll beat that Eight-Six and
 make you eat your words.

00:02:53.100 --> 00:03:00.550
The R32 Skyline GT-R and I will
 humiliate Akina's downhill specialist !

00:03:08.050 --> 00:03:10.240
You'll understand once you race against it.

00:03:26.600 --> 00:03:29.400
<b><i>New Movie [Initial]</i></b>

00:03:26.600 --> 00:03:29.400
<i>Central Anime</i>

00:03:26.600 --> 00:03:29.400
<b><i>- Racer -</i></b>

00:03:36.900 --> 00:03:39.700
Don't spill it, or you'll squish the tofu.

00:03:41.500 --> 00:03:42.200
More than usual ?

00:03:42.770 --> 00:03:44.600
You have a big load today.

00:03:58.830 --> 00:04:03.390
I thought he had changed a bit, 
but maybe it's just my imagination.

00:04:05.900 --> 00:04:08.550
GENERAL

00:04:07.250 --> 00:04:08.490
This way, please.

00:04:10.550 --> 00:04:11.890
Thank you so much.

00:04:13.060 --> 00:04:16.330
Takahashi Ryosuke was in Akina, huh ?

00:04:16.330 --> 00:04:18.650
He had super precise drift.

00:04:18.650 --> 00:04:21.930
But what surprised me more was the GT-R.

00:04:21.930 --> 00:04:26.460
The driver showed excellent grip,
 and stayed right on the FC's tail.

00:04:26.460 --> 00:04:28.400
I don't know who it was, but he's amazing.

00:04:28.900 --> 00:04:34.920
Well, drifting is flashy, but some say
 it's slower than driving with grip.

00:04:34.920 --> 00:04:37.530
Is that so, Iketani ?

00:04:37.530 --> 00:04:41.900
But real drifting is fast, and Takumi proved it.

00:04:44.120 --> 00:04:47.600
Did you think about it, Takumi ?

00:04:47.600 --> 00:04:48.400
Well...

00:04:48.400 --> 00:04:54.450
I beg you. I got carried away, and said your 
Eight-Six was the Akina Speed Stars' secret weapon.

00:04:54.450 --> 00:04:57.010
{minna}I already blew my horn.

00:04:57.010 --> 00:05:00.790
Same here.
 We'll be embarrassed if you don't join.

00:05:00.790 --> 00:05:06.160
You have to join, Takumi. 
I'm a part of the deal.

00:05:06.900 --> 00:05:12.800
I don't mind joining your team, 
but it's for street racers, right ?

00:05:13.120 --> 00:05:16.200
{ore}But I'm not a street racer, so...

00:05:16.700 --> 00:05:18.680
What the hell are you talking about ?

00:05:18.680 --> 00:05:22.100
Nobody drives faster than you in Akina.

00:05:23.260 --> 00:05:24.460
Is that so...?

00:05:25.200 --> 00:05:29.700
It is. If you're not a 
street racer, what are you ?!

00:05:29.700 --> 00:05:33.100
A cup of water is a nice idea.

00:05:33.100 --> 00:05:41.120
I thought Takumi's superb driving was because of his
 experience in driving Akina's downhill for so long, but...

00:05:41.820 --> 00:05:43.650
{chigau}...I was wrong.

00:05:43.650 --> 00:05:46.050
The uphill drive was more important.

00:05:46.050 --> 00:05:49.200
The load shift is one of the basics of controlling a car.

00:05:49.200 --> 00:05:55.800
{koppu}If you try not to spill water in a cup,
 you'll learn extremely sensitive load shifting.

00:05:55.800 --> 00:05:57.800
{suge}You're amazing, Bunta.

00:05:57.800 --> 00:06:01.800
You've trained him into a 
completely new type of driver. {<OVERLAP> BUNTA Thank you.}

00:05:58.900 --> 00:05:59.920
 Thank you.

00:06:18.990 --> 00:06:20.700
That was quite a circus.

00:06:21.600 --> 00:06:23.850
I hate drifters...

00:06:23.850 --> 00:06:26.040
...but that Eight-Six was fast.

00:06:28.830 --> 00:06:34.570
I need a neck and neck battle 
where I can lose myself completely.

00:06:35.310 --> 00:06:38.300
You'll be a worthy opponent...

00:06:39.500 --> 00:06:40.950
...Akina's Eight-Six.

00:06:47.200 --> 00:06:48.390
So hot...

00:06:49.390 --> 00:06:55.300
I wish I could take deliveries in an
 air-conditioned car, like Iketani and Takumi.

00:06:56.520 --> 00:06:59.800
I just don't understand Takumi.

00:07:00.200 --> 00:07:03.250
He totally owned Takahashi 
Keisuke of the Akagi Red Suns.

00:07:04.450 --> 00:07:09.210
But he hasn't changed a bit, and doesn't
 even think of himself as a street racer.

00:07:09.910 --> 00:07:16.290
I'd be so hyped up, telling everyone
 in school how I did this and...

00:07:18.000 --> 00:07:19.000
Welcome.

00:07:23.060 --> 00:07:25.570
A GT-R ! How awesome !

00:07:29.290 --> 00:07:32.700
I'm Nakazato of the Myogi Night Kids.

00:07:32.700 --> 00:07:38.800
I was told by the locals that I could 
contact the Akina Speed Stars here.

00:07:38.800 --> 00:07:40.000
You're a member, aren't you ?

00:07:40.000 --> 00:07:40.690
Huh ?

00:07:41.300 --> 00:07:46.380
Can you tell me when I should visit 
Akina to see that famous Eight-Six ?

00:07:49.020 --> 00:07:51.900
A Speed Stars member...

00:07:51.900 --> 00:07:55.060
That sounds so cool.

00:07:56.030 --> 00:07:58.650
Hey, do you know what I'm talking about ?

00:07:58.650 --> 00:08:00.490
Maybe this's the wrong gas station.

00:08:00.490 --> 00:08:02.750
No, you got the right station.

00:08:02.750 --> 00:08:06.620
In fact, the Eight-Six driver
 is a close friend of mine.

00:08:06.620 --> 00:08:07.680
Really ?

00:08:07.680 --> 00:08:13.390
He and I are the fastest 
Eight-Six duo among the members.

00:08:13.390 --> 00:08:14.300
Is that right ?

00:08:15.010 --> 00:08:19.900
Many Eight-Six drivers are very skilled, 
and I hear good things about the Speed Stars.

00:08:20.630 --> 00:08:23.670
I'm so honored.

00:08:23.670 --> 00:08:26.700
Anyway, I can get a hold of him.

00:08:26.700 --> 00:08:29.250
He's my best friend after all.

00:08:29.880 --> 00:08:32.040
Thanks. 
Make sure you tell him...

00:08:32.800 --> 00:08:38.150
...Nakazato of the Night Kids will be waiting on Mt. Akina at 10 pm next Saturday...

00:08:38.150 --> 00:08:40.570
{shobu}...for one downhill match.

00:08:44.000 --> 00:08:47.630
Wha...? 
W...wait ! Please...

00:08:54.000 --> 00:08:56.200
Holy crap...

00:08:56.200 --> 00:08:57.100
That was...

00:08:58.700 --> 00:09:00.700
...a declaration of challenge !

00:09:02.890 --> 00:09:06.900
I'm sorry ! 
So sorry, really sorry !

00:09:06.900 --> 00:09:08.000
I apologize !

00:09:09.660 --> 00:09:11.750
What a pain.

00:09:11.750 --> 00:09:15.200
It must be the black GT-R we saw on Akina.

00:09:15.200 --> 00:09:16.700
It's gotta be.

00:09:16.700 --> 00:09:22.000
It makes sense. Nakazato of the Night Kids can stack up against Takahashi Ryosuke.

00:09:23.260 --> 00:09:29.500
Takumi, I'm not in a place to be asking this,
 but will you accept his challenge ?

00:09:30.580 --> 00:09:33.150
Otherwise, I'll be a burden to them.

00:09:33.150 --> 00:09:38.600
I don't get it. Why would you be
 a burden to them if I don't go ?

00:09:39.040 --> 00:09:42.080
People'll speak bad about the 
Speed Stars for running away.

00:09:42.080 --> 00:09:43.200
Street racers...

00:09:44.650 --> 00:09:49.370
{hashiriya}When it comes to a car race, 
street racers must accept challenges !

00:09:50.300 --> 00:09:54.430
If you like to drive a car,
 that's enough to be a street racer !

00:09:56.020 --> 00:10:01.660
That may be true for street racers, 
but I'm not a street racer.

00:10:05.900 --> 00:10:06.730
Welcome.

00:10:07.500 --> 00:10:08.730
Hey, Takumi...

00:10:09.260 --> 00:10:14.010
Iketani, what should we do ?
 We'll be in trouble if Takumi doesn't go.

00:10:14.990 --> 00:10:20.820
Well, the GT-R would be
 too tough, even for Takumi.

00:10:21.890 --> 00:10:28.430
Besides, Nakazato of Myogi is a famous street racer just like Akagi's Takahashi brothers.

00:10:28.430 --> 00:10:31.330
{sore}Given the circumstances,
 I can't force him into this.

00:11:21.100 --> 00:11:25.260
Dad, is the GT-R really that good ?

00:11:26.790 --> 00:11:29.180
Yeah, it is.

00:11:29.180 --> 00:11:31.520
Could you beat it on the downhill ?

00:11:31.520 --> 00:11:33.040
I could.

00:11:34.740 --> 00:11:38.000
It's a piece of cake, 
whether it's a GT-R or a Porsche.

00:11:39.240 --> 00:11:41.500
You think I can defeat it ?

00:11:42.030 --> 00:11:44.300
You want me to lend you my car ?

00:11:47.400 --> 00:11:49.000
No, it's okay.

00:11:49.900 --> 00:11:50.870
I see.

00:11:56.550 --> 00:11:58.010
Thanks for the food.

00:12:07.050 --> 00:12:08.910
So a GT-R will be next, huh ?

00:12:12.300 --> 00:12:14.500
Nakazato's GT-R is here again today !

00:12:15.350 --> 00:12:18.000
Its exit acceleration is incredible !
 How much horsepower does it have ?

00:12:20.760 --> 00:12:25.360
It's going to race against the Speed Star's Eight-Six tomorrow, right ? That's all they're talking about.

00:12:25.360 --> 00:12:27.200
I smell trouble.

00:12:27.200 --> 00:12:33.200
The Night Kids' Nakazato is challenging the Eight-Six, which defeated the Red Suns' Takahashi Keisuke.

00:12:33.850 --> 00:12:38.630
It's going to be a clash of pride between
 the two large factions of Akagi and Myogi.

00:12:39.540 --> 00:12:42.110
Akina's nights are gonna
 be super exciting this summer.

00:12:49.650 --> 00:12:52.670
That Civic that just went by was really fast.

00:12:57.020 --> 00:13:02.200
Sure, the GT-R is a monster, but it's not invincible.

00:13:08.790 --> 00:13:12.350
Itsuki, I've thought about it since then.

00:13:12.350 --> 00:13:16.600
I'm going to ask Takumi to race tonight.

00:13:18.800 --> 00:13:24.600
Even if his opponent is a GT-R, the Eight-Six 
becomes something else with Takumi behind the wheel.

00:13:24.600 --> 00:13:27.000
It turns into an amazing super machine.

00:13:28.350 --> 00:13:30.400
I don't think he'll listen.

00:13:30.400 --> 00:13:31.310
What ?

00:13:31.310 --> 00:13:37.800
He's hated being forced or told
 what to do since he was little.

00:13:39.200 --> 00:13:43.500
He looks reserved, but he's really stubborn.

00:13:44.190 --> 00:13:47.180
He's that type.

00:13:47.400 --> 00:13:48.400
I see.

00:13:49.170 --> 00:13:54.600
Iketani, I'll go to Mt. Akina tonight, 
and apologize to the GT-R driver.

00:13:54.600 --> 00:13:55.300
Itsuki...

00:13:56.000 --> 00:13:59.300
I'll explain the circumstances, 
and kneel down on the ground or whatever.

00:13:59.300 --> 00:14:02.950
{motomoto}{Originally, this has nothing to do with}From the beginning, the
 Speed Stars had nothing to do with this.

00:14:04.130 --> 00:14:06.600
Alright, we'll go too.

00:14:06.600 --> 00:14:09.000
Don't mention this to Takumi.

00:14:09.000 --> 00:14:11.280
He must have forgotten about it already.

00:14:12.520 --> 00:14:14.670
Speaking of which, where's Takumi ?

00:14:14.670 --> 00:14:16.300
Oh, he's in the office.

00:14:16.300 --> 00:14:19.010
The Manager{Master} had something to discuss with him.

00:14:20.340 --> 00:14:22.590
Let me make this clear{remind you}, Takumi.

00:14:23.000 --> 00:14:26.000
You shouldn't do this because
 the GT-R is a nasty opponent.

00:14:27.790 --> 00:14:31.900
You're only doing this
to save face for Itsuki, right?

00:14:31.900 --> 00:14:33.650
If so, you shouldn't.

00:14:34.390 --> 00:14:40.900
You're clueless about cars, so you don't know how great the GT-R is, like a class of its own.

00:14:41.660 --> 00:14:48.810
It's got the combined advantage of FR and 4WD thanks to the electrically-controlled torque-split 4WD system.

00:14:49.340 --> 00:14:52.680
It's also fast on the downhill because of superb stability.

00:14:52.680 --> 00:14:57.240
The RB26 twin turbo engine is monstrous.

00:14:57.240 --> 00:15:04.500
It was originally designed to make 600 HP for racing,
 so you can easily obtain power with a minor modification. {FYI, the stock power is 280}

00:15:07.740 --> 00:15:10.020
The Eight-Six is totally outclassed.

00:15:10.800 --> 00:15:15.500
Besides, your opponent is a famous
 street racer. This race is really unfair.

00:15:16.500 --> 00:15:22.870
You made a name by defeating the
 Akagi Red Suns, so you'd better cherish it.

00:15:22.870 --> 00:15:26.530
You gain nothing by participating in
 a race you have no chance of winning.

00:15:27.760 --> 00:15:30.950
Listen to your elders{adults}, okay ?

00:15:33.100 --> 00:15:36.250
Thank you for your advice, but...

00:15:37.000 --> 00:15:43.000
...I'm not really interested in being a 
famous street racer or anything like that.

00:15:45.150 --> 00:15:47.600
So you're not going to back down ?

00:15:49.090 --> 00:15:50.790
I won't.

00:15:50.790 --> 00:15:57.500
If you hype it up like that, I want to
 find out how great that car really is.

00:15:58.330 --> 00:16:01.920
Manager{ster}, I'm not afraid of the GT-R.

00:16:16.030 --> 00:16:17.400
He bought it.

00:16:17.650 --> 00:16:21.450
I can't remember how many
 times I fooled Bunta this way.

00:16:21.450 --> 00:16:25.550
They're so alike, right 
down to their personality.

00:16:25.550 --> 00:16:28.650
This is going to be fun.

00:16:30.800 --> 00:16:32.800
Temporarily Closed 
for Personal Reasons
 -Fujiwara Tofu Shop

00:16:33.410 --> 00:16:35.350
Temporarily closed, what the hell ?

00:16:35.350 --> 00:16:36.600
{kiite}I didn't know about this.

00:16:37.650 --> 00:16:40.070
We're poor, you can't be slacking off.

00:16:43.850 --> 00:16:45.010
Where is the car ?

00:16:53.160 --> 00:16:54.140
Dad ?

00:17:01.160 --> 00:17:03.900
I can't do anything without the car.

00:17:21.670 --> 00:17:23.510
Such a huge gallery.

00:17:23.510 --> 00:17:26.540
It looks bigger than the one during the race against Takahashi Keisuke the other day.

00:17:27.540 --> 00:17:31.000
I didn't expect this to become such a huge event.

00:17:48.990 --> 00:17:51.760
The black GT-R's Nakazato...

00:17:51.760 --> 00:17:55.070
A huge group of the Night Kids members came.

00:17:57.700 --> 00:18:02.480
This isn't the atmosphere{mood} for admitting mistakes.

00:18:14.230 --> 00:18:15.900
The Takahashi brothers have come.

00:18:15.900 --> 00:18:19.290
Hurry up !
Keisuke is so cool !

00:18:19.290 --> 00:18:21.760
Ryosuke, you're so gorgeous !

00:18:29.760 --> 00:18:32.110
Takahashi Ryosuke and Keisuke have come, too ?

00:18:32.110 --> 00:18:35.000
That makes it even harder to back off. 
What should we do ?

00:18:50.970 --> 00:18:55.830
Why am I so irritated ?
 I want to go so bad.

00:18:57.200 --> 00:19:01.490
If you like to drive a car,
 that's enough to be a street racer !

00:19:01.490 --> 00:19:04.760
If you're a street racer, 
be proud of the skills you've got !

00:19:06.400 --> 00:19:11.900
I don't know if I like to drive or not, but...

00:19:11.900 --> 00:19:16.950
...I am proud of the skills I've learned by myself.

00:19:18.000 --> 00:19:24.730
At least, I feel like that, and I want 
to test my skills to the limit.

00:19:24.730 --> 00:19:30.030
{ore}I want to challenge the GT-R 
by throwing everything I've got at it.

00:19:31.260 --> 00:19:35.790
I've never felt this way.
 I'm getting eager to drive.

00:19:37.300 --> 00:19:40.850
Dad, please come home.

00:19:49.700 --> 00:19:50.370
That's...

00:19:57.910 --> 00:19:58.790
That sound.

00:20:02.000 --> 00:20:03.060
I'm off, Dad !

00:20:07.040 --> 00:20:09.140
His eyes looked different.

00:20:17.660 --> 00:20:20.400
The Takahashi brothers have come as expected.

00:20:22.720 --> 00:20:26.920
They must be concerned.
 I was assured I'd lose.

00:20:27.640 --> 00:20:36.610
This's a great opportunity for us to show the gallery that drifting can never be faster than gripping.

00:20:36.610 --> 00:20:41.060
Oh man. Here comes 
Takeshi's tunnel-minded opinion.

00:20:41.060 --> 00:20:43.000
Shut up. You know it's true.

00:20:43.900 --> 00:20:48.110
Drift is just a performance to please the gallery.

00:20:48.110 --> 00:20:51.500
{hayasa}It's meaningless to be a street 
 racer if you don't try to drive fast.

00:20:52.590 --> 00:20:56.140
I know it because I used to drift.

00:20:56.140 --> 00:21:01.700
Once you're done with drifting and start
 driving with grip, you'll know it's better.

00:21:01.700 --> 00:21:05.490
The time of the drifting FR is over.

00:21:05.490 --> 00:21:09.540
I'll put an end to Akina's Eight-Six.

00:21:13.280 --> 00:21:14.800
Itsuki, let's go.

00:21:15.650 --> 00:21:17.900
We'll be with you.

00:21:18.650 --> 00:21:21.200
I don't know what they're 
going to do to you, but...

00:21:22.630 --> 00:21:28.200
They'll kill me if I say the Eight-Six won't come.

00:21:29.540 --> 00:21:34.400
Father, Mother...
 God help me, please.

00:21:34.400 --> 00:21:37.650
I've never slept with a girl !

00:21:38.650 --> 00:21:41.390
I don't wanna die !

00:21:53.600 --> 00:21:57.170
Why are you kneeling down
right in the middle of the road ?

00:21:58.300 --> 00:21:59.350
Takumi...

00:22:04.170 --> 00:22:06.680
Takumi, you came.

00:22:09.900 --> 00:22:12.060
Sorry I'm late, Itsuki.

00:22:13.140 --> 00:22:17.700
When it comes to a car race, 
street racers must accept challenges, right ?

00:22:21.990 --> 00:22:23.850
Takumi !

00:22:26.750 --> 00:22:28.230
There he is, Takeshi.

00:22:29.410 --> 00:22:34.420
So pretentious, showing up at the last moment.

00:22:35.120 --> 00:22:38.600
I thought he'd be older.

00:22:38.600 --> 00:22:43.390
How did a kid like him acquire such technique ?

00:22:53.150 --> 00:22:55.400
Your Eight-Six is gone.

00:22:55.400 --> 00:22:56.680
Yuichi ?!

00:22:56.680 --> 00:22:59.430
Takumi went to Mt. Akina ?

00:22:59.430 --> 00:23:05.190
Yeah, he took off looking really uptight.
 I don't know what's going on.

00:23:05.190 --> 00:23:09.100
{aitsu}I never expected him to go
 to the mountain pass himself.

00:23:09.500 --> 00:23:12.300
Like father, like son, after all.

00:23:13.200 --> 00:23:18.250
Bunta, he'll be racing against a GT-R. 
Did you give him any advice ?

00:23:19.010 --> 00:23:20.390
Nothing really.

00:23:22.580 --> 00:23:23.300
But...

00:23:23.760 --> 00:23:25.660
But what ?

00:23:34.370 --> 00:23:37.000
This is the goal. 
All marshals are in position.

00:23:37.700 --> 00:23:41.210
Nobody's entered the mountain pass. 
We can start any time.

00:23:41.210 --> 00:23:43.900
Roger that. 
Let us know if someone else enters.

00:23:43.900 --> 00:23:44.500
Got it.

00:23:45.000 --> 00:23:47.650
I'm Nakazato of the Myogi Night Kids.

00:23:47.650 --> 00:23:48.550
Your name ?

00:23:49.400 --> 00:23:50.880
Fujiwara Takumi.

00:23:51.600 --> 00:23:53.700
I'll remember your name.

00:24:02.730 --> 00:24:05.650
Start counting down in five...

00:24:05.650 --> 00:24:06.550
Four...

00:24:06.550 --> 00:24:07.490
Three...

00:24:07.490 --> 00:24:08.370
Two...

00:24:08.370 --> 00:24:09.380
One...

00:24:09.380 --> 00:24:10.030
Go !

00:24:13.210 --> 00:24:15.150
Takumi, go for it !

00:24:19.440 --> 00:24:25.550
I'll let you enjoy the Cinderella Castle Mystery Tour from the best seat in the house, Keisuke.

00:24:33.200 --> 00:24:36.700
Nakazato's going easy on the
 gas to wait for the Eight-Six.

00:24:37.620 --> 00:24:40.000
It's meaningless to 
out-accelerate him on a straightaway.

00:24:40.000 --> 00:24:45.460
{orewa}I want a battle.
 The real start begins in the corner.

00:24:49.450 --> 00:24:51.000
You've gotta be kidding !

00:24:51.000 --> 00:24:55.670
There's no way you can stay behind me with that overly showy crab-like driving !

00:25:08.100 --> 00:25:10.000
I'm impressed.

00:25:10.000 --> 00:25:15.350
Watching his driving this close,
 it reminds me that his drift is an art.

00:25:15.350 --> 00:25:19.900
Even I can't control my FC like that at the limit.

00:25:19.900 --> 00:25:24.090
But wouldn't a non-turbo Eight-Six eventually lose because of the lack of power ?

00:25:24.090 --> 00:25:33.160
A turbo is a powerful aid in straightaways, but its
 power will make the car unstable at the exit of corners.

00:25:33.160 --> 00:25:34.170
It's a double-edge sword.

00:25:37.450 --> 00:25:41.150
But once you get the Eight-Six at the right angle, you can step on the gas as you like.

00:25:41.650 --> 00:25:46.990
In a technical course, an under-powered car can be faster if you can be aggressive on the accelerator.

00:25:48.020 --> 00:25:56.100
Come to think of it, I could barely use the full 
throttle of my 350 HP engine on Akina's downhill.

00:25:56.100 --> 00:25:59.100
You go boom, and you have to brake right after.

00:25:59.100 --> 00:26:01.200
{partial}It was also frustrating that I had 
to use partial throttle so often.{quite a lot.}

00:26:01.200 --> 00:26:05.650
That's the nature of the FR layout.

00:26:06.210 --> 00:26:08.000
Nature of the FR ?

00:26:08.650 --> 00:26:12.100
Wait, Brother ! 
What about the GT-R's 4WD ?!

00:26:12.670 --> 00:26:19.060
Its ATTESA E-TS can let you step on the gas without losing control, so you can use the turbo power as much as you like.

00:26:29.820 --> 00:26:30.900
This is it.

00:26:31.650 --> 00:26:37.000
This feeling of high tension, like
 the blood in my entire body is boiling.

00:26:37.000 --> 00:26:38.500
This is a battle !

00:26:41.650 --> 00:26:43.050
The Eight-Six is falling behind.

00:26:44.050 --> 00:26:47.500
Nakazato may be a big talker, but he's good.

00:26:47.900 --> 00:26:51.500
He minimizes the under-steer by 
transferring the weight skillfully.

00:26:51.500 --> 00:26:54.500
It's the type of driving that
makes use of the GT-R's power.

00:26:54.500 --> 00:26:58.000
{omoshiromi}It looks boring, but he doesn't drive wastefully, giving no overtaking opportunities.{It looks boring, but the defense is 
tight because the style is efficient.}

00:26:58.820 --> 00:27:01.590
You can't be so relaxed, Brother.

00:27:01.590 --> 00:27:06.870
It'd be humiliating to allow the 
Night Kids to defeat the Eight-Six.

00:27:06.870 --> 00:27:08.970
I doubt that will happen.

00:27:10.280 --> 00:27:14.750
The first half has many 
straightaways and the slopes are mild.

00:27:14.750 --> 00:27:19.620
The slope is steep in the second half, and that's where the downhill specialist will show his true potential.

00:27:31.050 --> 00:27:33.780
What amazing drift !

00:27:33.780 --> 00:27:35.820
That's Akina's Eight-Six.

00:27:35.820 --> 00:27:36.990
Incredible.

00:27:38.400 --> 00:27:39.670
{yume}This must be a dream !{at might appear in the dream.}

00:27:39.670 --> 00:27:41.150
Takahashi Ryosuke's FC ?!

00:27:41.150 --> 00:27:43.460
What's going on ? 
A three-way match ?

00:27:43.460 --> 00:27:48.430
Is this going to determine
 who's the fastest in Gunma ?!

00:27:54.100 --> 00:27:57.400
Low-speed hairpin curves 
are the GT-R's area of specialty.

00:27:59.260 --> 00:28:02.390
If you can use the powerful
 brakes to slow down like you should...

00:28:02.390 --> 00:28:05.710
{kudari}...the weight will shift to the front regardless.

00:28:05.710 --> 00:28:08.900
{saidai}The biggest weakness of losing 
front tire grip can be minimized. {Using the definition of gpush under,h which is to lose the grip during acceleration at the exit of a corner.}

00:28:10.080 --> 00:28:15.520
And this is the moment of truth.

00:28:15.520 --> 00:28:21.880
This acceleration from the low gear is unmatched, and the stiff body is steady as a rock.

00:28:22.340 --> 00:28:26.360
{circuit}The fastest machine on the circuit
 is the fastest on the public roads.

00:28:26.360 --> 00:28:30.300
{rear}The R badge on the rear right 
symbolizes the R's unbeaten legend.

00:28:30.860 --> 00:28:33.850
Can you keep up with my R, Eight-Six ?

00:28:36.240 --> 00:28:37.000
It's different...

00:28:39.650 --> 00:28:41.040
Something's different.

00:28:42.830 --> 00:28:45.850
You changed the suspension setting ?

00:28:45.850 --> 00:28:48.460
Heavy under-steer when you open the throttle.

00:28:48.460 --> 00:28:51.620
Heavy under-steer ? 
What're you thinking, Bunta ?

00:28:51.620 --> 00:28:54.860
Takumi will have to drift. 
If the suspension is...

00:28:54.860 --> 00:28:56.760
You don't know anything.

00:28:56.760 --> 00:29:03.000
When it comes to the FR, a skilled driver can 
maintain full throttle longer because of under-steering.

00:29:04.090 --> 00:29:05.650
It's even more true when drifting.

00:29:08.400 --> 00:29:11.210
I didn't tell Takumi about it, though...

00:29:11.210 --> 00:29:17.060
You didn't ? He must be freaked out by 
now because of it's different handling.{ differently.}

00:29:17.060 --> 00:29:25.460
It's pointless to tell him because he's not smart enough to change his driving style after thinking it through.

00:29:25.460 --> 00:29:27.000
If that's the case...

00:29:27.610 --> 00:29:32.630
He may not be smart, but what
 he's learned with his body is real.

00:29:32.630 --> 00:29:36.480
Minor modifications to the 
suspension won't bother him.

00:29:36.480 --> 00:29:37.910
Bunta...

00:29:39.040 --> 00:29:41.440
Takumi should be able to figure it out.

00:29:41.440 --> 00:29:44.650
The Eight-Six is the type of car 
that can train the driver after all.

00:29:48.420 --> 00:29:51.040
It's different.
 It's definitely different.

00:29:53.530 --> 00:29:55.650
The car remains stable when
 I'm pressing harder on the pedal.

00:29:55.650 --> 00:29:58.760
{imamade}I can start pressing the pedal a bit earlier.

00:29:59.640 --> 00:30:02.680
{nagare}I don't have to hesitate because
 the car doesn't skid too much.

00:30:02.680 --> 00:30:04.800
{sokka}I see it, Dad.

00:30:05.650 --> 00:30:08.500
This is why you closed the shop.

00:30:09.660 --> 00:30:13.390
I don't know how it works, but it feels good.

00:30:24.370 --> 00:30:26.950
Amazing. 
My eyes can barely keep up.

00:30:29.750 --> 00:30:31.000
I lost to that technique.

00:30:31.700 --> 00:30:34.500
He started to drop the
 inside tire into the gutter.

00:30:35.080 --> 00:30:39.310
He must have gotten serious. 
He's going nuts.

00:30:44.910 --> 00:30:46.850
The Eight-Six is gaining on me !

00:30:46.850 --> 00:30:48.150
 Ridiculous !

00:30:48.150 --> 00:30:48.990
That's impossible !

00:31:02.820 --> 00:31:04.400
Very well done.

00:31:04.400 --> 00:31:10.320
My presumption about the Eight-Six being an
 under-powered classic is gone if you can push it that hard.

00:31:10.320 --> 00:31:14.000
{ikkyuu}It's a wonderful machine with
top-notch combat potential.

00:31:15.370 --> 00:31:17.650
{zokuzoku}I'm so thrilled.

00:31:17.650 --> 00:31:21.540
I haven't had an exciting battle 
like this since I switched to this car.

00:31:32.820 --> 00:31:36.550
In low-speed corners, even though the Eight-Six can almost bite the GT-R's tail during the entry...

00:31:36.550 --> 00:31:39.650
{tachiagari}...the gap widens at the exit because
 of the difference in initial acceleration.

00:31:42.300 --> 00:31:45.800
{daga}But in high-speed corners,
 the Eight-Six can narrow the gap.

00:31:48.540 --> 00:31:53.250
The street racers all talk about having to aim at the very inside of the corners, but he's extraordinary.

00:31:58.060 --> 00:32:00.800
The bumper almost rubs the guard rails...

00:32:00.800 --> 00:32:04.700
{genkai}...as the car takes the shortest path while 
drifting with four wheels at its limit.{ speed.}

00:32:05.650 --> 00:32:10.400
In order for the under-powered Eight-Six to
 maintain speed he avoids wasteful deceleration.

00:32:10.400 --> 00:32:12.720
{mudana}That's why he uses drift.

00:32:16.000 --> 00:32:21.440
He's in a class of his own. This has 
nothing to do with vehicle performance.

00:32:21.440 --> 00:32:24.990
{ano}That bastard must have a few screws loose !

00:32:31.100 --> 00:32:33.290
His pressure is tremendous.

00:32:33.290 --> 00:32:35.320
Why can't I shake it ?

00:32:35.650 --> 00:32:38.760
Dammit !
 I'm so glad to be alive !

00:32:44.860 --> 00:32:47.730
I wonder where Takumi is at right now ?

00:32:47.730 --> 00:32:52.000
Given the incredible speed,
 he must have gone down quite far.

00:32:56.200 --> 00:32:59.060
If that Eight-Six turns out
 to be a worthy opponent...

00:32:59.060 --> 00:33:03.000
{sorosoro}...the GT-R's weakness will 
hit Takeshi just about now.

00:33:04.880 --> 00:33:08.610
The GT-R's weakness ? What's that ?

00:33:08.610 --> 00:33:11.560
Simply put, the body weight.

00:33:11.560 --> 00:33:13.000
Body weight ?

00:33:14.310 --> 00:33:19.430
The GT-R's weakness is under-steering
 because of its super heavy front section.

00:33:19.430 --> 00:33:22.150
Even if you try to mitigate it 
with tuning or driving technique...

00:33:22.150 --> 00:33:24.360
{kihon}...you can't change the basic characteristics.

00:33:24.360 --> 00:33:30.720
If you continue a forceful steering manner as you use the ABS on the hard downhill...

00:33:30.720 --> 00:33:34.150
{kanarazu}...the front tires and brakes will lose their grip.

00:33:35.160 --> 00:33:41.720
By the time you reach the bottom, you'll be 
fighting under-steering at the entrance of corners.

00:33:42.720 --> 00:33:45.440
Even with a well-tuned brake system.

00:33:52.420 --> 00:33:56.870
The response from the front has become dull. 
It's slightly under-steering.

00:33:57.760 --> 00:34:01.250
The stress to the front 
tires was greater than expected.

00:34:02.110 --> 00:34:03.110
This is gonna be tough.

00:34:03.650 --> 00:34:06.480
But I must not lose !

00:34:13.600 --> 00:34:14.600
{Over there}They're here !

00:34:15.000 --> 00:34:16.900
The Eight-Six is right on its tail !

00:34:16.900 --> 00:34:19.510
Nakazato's the fastest in Myogi, 
but he's being pressed hard !{ yet he's in a pinch.}

00:34:21.000 --> 00:34:25.900
I saw you overtake Takahashi 
Keisuke in these five hairpin curves.

00:34:26.670 --> 00:34:31.820
You only have to keep the inside closed. I'll never open the inside no matter what.

00:34:34.360 --> 00:34:35.200
What the...?

00:34:35.680 --> 00:34:37.210
From the outside ?!

00:34:42.050 --> 00:34:44.030
Don't screw around with me, you brat !

00:34:44.990 --> 00:34:46.070
Did you see that ?

00:34:46.070 --> 00:34:49.790
That was insane. 
It drifted through this narrow road.

00:34:51.010 --> 00:34:52.040
From the outside again ?

00:34:52.650 --> 00:34:54.040
It's so annoying !

00:34:56.140 --> 00:35:01.170
The GT-R's motion is unstable. 
Nakazato must be losing concentration.

00:35:02.150 --> 00:35:05.500
Keisuke, the Eight-Six's going
 to overtake, so don't miss it !

00:35:10.820 --> 00:35:11.650
I see.

00:35:16.900 --> 00:35:21.950
{yatsu}I can enter the corners a little faster if I leave just enough space that's too narrow for him to pass.

00:35:21.950 --> 00:35:24.700
{out}He's taking the outer line, 
which means he won't take the inside !

00:35:28.290 --> 00:35:30.580
It's gone. Where...where is it?

00:35:34.720 --> 00:35:36.000
The outer line was a feint motion !

00:35:37.300 --> 00:35:39.490
 He changed his line while full braking{ full } ?!

00:35:41.000 --> 00:35:44.100
That was a brilliant move, but...

00:35:44.100 --> 00:35:48.300
{konomama}...starting from side-by-side, I can still pull 
ahead using full acceleration in second gear.

00:35:48.920 --> 00:35:52.460
I'll show you the true potential of the RB26 !

00:36:16.490 --> 00:36:20.160
It lost...?
The GT-R lost...

00:36:23.360 --> 00:36:26.900
No, that's not it. 
I'm the one who lost.

00:36:28.350 --> 00:36:32.660
The GT-R didn't lose to the Eight-Six.

00:36:32.660 --> 00:36:38.120
It's a shock, but somehow it feels good.

00:36:38.120 --> 00:36:40.700
I did everything I could.

00:36:42.050 --> 00:36:45.590
There're plenty of great drivers out there.

00:36:45.590 --> 00:36:48.200
{touge}And there's quite a few of them
 driving the mountain passes.{a lot of
 them in{to the} {mountain pass driving.}

00:36:50.900 --> 00:36:53.370
That was fun, wasn't it, Keisuke ?

00:36:53.370 --> 00:36:55.100
That was great.

00:36:55.100 --> 00:36:57.800
It pressured the GT-R really 
hard during braking on the downhill.

00:36:57.800 --> 00:37:01.100
The Eight-Six must have
high-performance ABS.

00:37:02.970 --> 00:37:06.700
What're you talking about ? 
You think the Eight-Six has ABS ?

00:37:07.480 --> 00:37:11.400
The driver's right foot is superior
to machine-controlled ABS.

00:37:13.250 --> 00:37:18.600
I haven't been this excited in a long time. 
I have to rewrite a big chunk of my paper.

00:37:19.800 --> 00:37:24.800
That Eight-Six is a really worthy target to defeat.

00:37:26.780 --> 00:37:27.760
Brother...

00:37:30.610 --> 00:37:32.660
T...Takumi...

00:37:32.660 --> 00:37:34.630
...won ?!

00:37:34.630 --> 00:37:35.590
Are you serious ?

00:37:35.590 --> 00:37:36.900
I'm checking now.

00:37:36.900 --> 00:37:38.130
Apparently, it's true.

00:37:38.130 --> 00:37:39.090
It can't be true.

00:37:39.090 --> 00:37:40.210
No way.

00:38:02.100 --> 00:38:06.210
Looks like you are the one
 who was humiliated, Takeshi.

00:38:06.210 --> 00:38:09.130
You can't act tough for quite a while.

00:38:09.130 --> 00:38:16.000
When I defeat the Eight-Six, then I, Shoji Shingo, will become the leader of the Night Kids.

00:38:16.600 --> 00:38:23.560
Just wait, Eight-Six. I'll send you to the junk yard by fighting under emotional, yet dangerous rules.

00:38:35.280 --> 00:38:36.000
Eat one.

00:38:36.630 --> 00:38:37.630
Thank you.

00:38:40.250 --> 00:38:41.000
Hot...

00:38:44.990 --> 00:38:51.120
This is awkward.
 I've begun to look at you differently.

00:38:51.120 --> 00:38:53.150
Huh ? What do you mean ?

00:38:53.800 --> 00:38:56.120
Right now, you're the usual Takumi.

00:38:56.120 --> 00:39:00.500
But once you get in the Eight-Six and are 
thrust into the night mountain pass...

00:39:00.500 --> 00:39:04.310
{imaya}...you become an admirable
 hero of Akina's street racers.

00:39:04.310 --> 00:39:06.650
Huh ? Really ?

00:39:06.650 --> 00:39:09.950
That's what this is all about ?
 You make me feel embarrassed, Itsuki.

00:39:09.950 --> 00:39:13.210
Although you're just an airhead
 munching on a sweet bun right now.

00:39:13.210 --> 00:39:14.800
"Airhead," you say ?

00:39:16.180 --> 00:39:20.060
I feel awkward, too.

00:39:20.060 --> 00:39:26.700
But if someone becomes happy because of what I do, that makes me really happy.

00:39:26.700 --> 00:39:31.700
I see. I didn't know you were the
 type who'd do things for others.

00:39:31.700 --> 00:39:36.000
Driving is slowly becoming fun.

00:39:37.110 --> 00:39:39.830
Iketani's car is repaired.

00:39:39.830 --> 00:39:41.450
That's good.

00:39:42.400 --> 00:39:45.330
Let's go to Akina tonight.

00:39:45.330 --> 00:39:46.070
Sure. {this can be omitted}

00:40:10.600 --> 00:40:12.870
You look happy.

00:40:12.870 --> 00:40:16.800
Of course. 
I finally got my baby back.

00:40:16.800 --> 00:40:18.500
The S13 Silvia, that is.

00:40:36.000 --> 00:40:36.750
When did it...?!

00:40:42.650 --> 00:40:44.430
It tapped my bumper.

00:40:45.030 --> 00:40:46.800
You want me to move because I'm too slow ?

00:40:46.800 --> 00:40:47.700
Screw you !

00:41:22.790 --> 00:41:25.090
T...Takumi...

00:41:25.090 --> 00:41:27.780
Itsuki, Iketani, are you alright ?

00:41:28.390 --> 00:41:30.300
I'm fine, more or less.

00:41:46.900 --> 00:41:49.630
Apologize ? 
You've gotta be kidding.

00:41:49.630 --> 00:41:50.700
Don't screw around with us !

00:41:50.700 --> 00:41:55.160
You hit us on purpose !
 You could have injured us really bad !

00:41:55.160 --> 00:42:00.650
Like I said before, it was your fault.

00:42:00.650 --> 00:42:03.870
{masaka}I didn't expect your corner entry to be so slow.

00:42:03.870 --> 00:42:07.170
No one could react fast 
enough to avoid a little bonk.

00:42:08.320 --> 00:42:09.660
Say what ?

00:42:09.660 --> 00:42:12.420
He's rubbing our nose in it.

00:42:12.420 --> 00:42:21.650
If you insist, I will kneel down and apologize only if
 you can defeat us in a downhill battle under our rules.

00:42:22.540 --> 00:42:26.660
{nannara}I don't mind if that Eight-Six
 driver over there is my opponent.

00:42:27.150 --> 00:42:29.400
You're good at the downhill, right ?

00:42:31.540 --> 00:42:33.240
What're you going to do ?

00:42:33.240 --> 00:42:39.000
So, are you Speed Stars boys in or not ?

00:42:39.800 --> 00:42:44.000
If you lose, you'll kneel 
down and apologize, right ?

00:42:44.500 --> 00:42:48.400
He's only provoking you, Takumi. 
You don't know what he might do.

00:42:48.900 --> 00:42:51.200
I won't lose to a guy like him, Iketani.

00:43:01.920 --> 00:43:06.210
Wait, you said something about rules.

00:43:06.210 --> 00:43:09.000
It's really not a big deal.

00:43:09.000 --> 00:43:12.140
We call it the gum tape{duct tape} death match.

00:43:12.140 --> 00:43:18.000
{migite}You tape your right hand
 to the steering wheel and race.

00:43:18.000 --> 00:43:19.300
That's all.

00:43:31.710 --> 00:43:33.880
Stop. Don't do this, Takumi.

00:43:33.880 --> 00:43:36.120
This's insane. It's so risky.

00:43:36.120 --> 00:43:38.200
You know what this means ?{ You can't}

00:43:38.200 --> 00:43:40.000
You can't steer as much !

00:43:41.100 --> 00:43:46.650
If you can't do that how are you
 going to clear the corners ?!

00:43:46.650 --> 00:43:49.510
But the conditions will be equal.

00:43:49.510 --> 00:43:53.930
He must have practiced !
That's why he brought up a rule like this !

00:43:53.930 --> 00:43:57.670
This's just too risky, even for you !
Please don't, Takumi !

00:43:57.670 --> 00:44:00.300
I won't quit, Iketani.

00:44:00.300 --> 00:44:04.060
I don't know why, but I don't want 
to lose to that guy no matter what.

00:44:05.650 --> 00:44:07.170
Takumi...

00:44:07.700 --> 00:44:10.300
You can go first, Eight-Six boy.

00:44:11.500 --> 00:44:12.000
Go !

00:44:16.550 --> 00:44:18.520
They're off.

00:44:18.520 --> 00:44:19.700
We've gotta go, too !

00:44:19.700 --> 00:44:21.420
Impossible !
 We'll never catch them !

00:44:22.090 --> 00:44:24.150
I'm not thinking about catching them !

00:44:24.150 --> 00:44:27.530
If Takumi crashes, I want to
 help him as soon as possible !

00:44:33.180 --> 00:44:36.300
There's no need for two downhill specialists.

00:44:36.300 --> 00:44:43.800
This EG6 Civic driver Shoji Shingo of the Myogi 
Night Kids is the fastest downhill driver in Gunma.

00:44:44.350 --> 00:44:47.300
Let's see how many corners you can clear.

00:44:56.460 --> 00:44:57.250
You're done.{over.}

00:45:11.500 --> 00:45:14.750
Damn, how did he recover from that ?

00:45:14.750 --> 00:45:16.100
But it's only a matter of time.

00:45:19.550 --> 00:45:25.600
No matter how good the driver is, you must apply a 
counter-steer to stop the over-steering of an FR car.

00:45:25.600 --> 00:45:29.480
Right, but the Civic is an FF, so...

00:45:29.480 --> 00:45:33.700
{over-steer}...you can stop over-steering with the accelerator, 
so you can dive into corners more aggressively.

00:45:33.700 --> 00:45:37.550
{side}And you can mitigate under-steering 
by pulling the parking brake.

00:45:37.550 --> 00:45:41.050
Under this rule, you'll crash
 unless you drive an FF car.

00:45:41.050 --> 00:45:46.010
If someone can avoid an accident
 in an FR car, he must be a monster.

00:45:49.520 --> 00:45:56.550
I feel so uneasy after every corner because
 I might see a wrecked Eight-Six at any moment.

00:45:57.300 --> 00:46:01.750
I feel like he's gonna be alright.
 It's Takumi, after all.

00:46:09.340 --> 00:46:11.590
Why ? Why can he turn ?

00:46:12.540 --> 00:46:16.200
The gum tape{duct tape} death match is not
 easy for a first timer to manage.

00:46:22.330 --> 00:46:25.810
See ? I can pass you
 any time if I want to.

00:46:27.200 --> 00:46:32.480
Why don't you feel the heat ?
 Attack harder and crash.

00:46:43.480 --> 00:46:45.650
I can go...

00:46:47.050 --> 00:46:48.090
...faster than usual.

00:46:58.210 --> 00:47:00.600
I can go faster if I depend less on the steering.

00:47:09.300 --> 00:47:10.650
What the hell ?

00:47:10.650 --> 00:47:13.350
No matter how much pressure 
I put on him, he remains stable.

00:47:13.350 --> 00:47:15.600
In fact, he's getting faster.

00:47:26.020 --> 00:47:29.630
I don't give a damn ! 
Victory is all that matters in a battle...

00:47:29.630 --> 00:47:31.650
{donna}...regardless of how !

00:47:48.390 --> 00:47:51.100
Damn, what a lucky ass brat.

00:47:51.100 --> 00:47:53.760
Well then, I'll just pull away right here !

00:47:56.650 --> 00:48:00.300
This is it. The sound of the engine
 revving all the way up to the red zone.

00:48:00.300 --> 00:48:04.600
{kono}I just can't get enough 
of this intoxicating feeling !

00:48:15.250 --> 00:48:17.200
You did that on purpose.

00:48:17.650 --> 00:48:22.750
I will not lose to a scumbag
 like you, no matter what !

00:48:43.630 --> 00:48:46.000
No way ! 
How can he keep up ?!

00:48:46.000 --> 00:48:48.850
I'm driving at my ultimate speed !

00:48:54.500 --> 00:48:57.500
What's going on with that Eight-Six ?

00:49:00.520 --> 00:49:01.900
He's not using the steering...

00:49:02.650 --> 00:49:05.000
...but turning by only shifting the weight !{the weight shift !}

00:49:31.850 --> 00:49:36.230
What the hell was that ?! 
How did he pass me in a place like that ?!

00:49:50.670 --> 00:49:54.000
If I lose the very gum{duct} 
tape death match I set up...

00:49:57.460 --> 00:50:01.820
...I'll be a laughingstock among my team members, and never be able to redeem myself.

00:50:02.600 --> 00:50:07.000
I have to save my rep even 
if that means I have to resort to a tie.

00:50:07.780 --> 00:50:12.240
The end of this battle is a double crash !

00:51:04.930 --> 00:51:06.370
My EG6...

00:51:30.100 --> 00:51:32.400
Ouch. You really blew it.{You've done it.}

00:51:34.400 --> 00:51:36.760
Hey, are you alright ? Are you hurt ?

00:51:38.010 --> 00:51:42.500
I think my right arm is broken because
 of the kickback from the steering wheel.

00:51:43.170 --> 00:51:49.070
Hop in. I'll take you to the hospital. 
It's faster than calling an ambulance.

00:51:49.070 --> 00:51:51.370
I can't owe you that much.

00:51:52.370 --> 00:51:53.450
Don't be so hard on yourself.

00:51:54.300 --> 00:51:58.350
It hurts, right ? 
 We'll take care of the mess here.

00:51:58.350 --> 00:52:00.200
We're used to things like this.

00:52:00.200 --> 00:52:04.450
Don't be a stranger.
 Crashes happen to anyone.

00:52:04.450 --> 00:52:07.210
We are locals, so we know
 the emergency hospital.

00:52:08.210 --> 00:52:09.870
As he says.

00:52:14.030 --> 00:52:16.350
Thanks, I owe you one.

00:52:23.400 --> 00:52:26.180
So Takumi won.

00:52:36.730 --> 00:52:39.000
He's incredible, isn't he ?

00:52:54.000 --> 00:52:59.300
I ended up facing a really annoying a-hole, 
and I snapped during the race.

00:52:59.300 --> 00:53:02.950
{sono}After that, I don't remember what happened.

00:53:02.950 --> 00:53:07.800
When we lose ourselves, both you
 and I don't know when to stop.

00:53:08.970 --> 00:53:11.850
{daga}But I'd never damage the car.

00:53:13.550 --> 00:53:16.000
So, did you win ?

00:53:17.830 --> 00:53:18.820
Yeah. {this can be omitted}

00:53:22.010 --> 00:53:23.150
I see.

00:53:25.920 --> 00:53:35.650
Like Itsuki and Iketani say, street racers 
love cars and take good care of them, but I...

00:53:42.650 --> 00:53:43.550
I'm sorry.

00:54:05.300 --> 00:54:07.500
It's worn out real bad.

00:54:09.640 --> 00:54:11.900
I might as well replace it while
 the car's in the body shop.

00:54:15.700 --> 00:54:17.510
It's hot again today.

00:54:22.730 --> 00:54:25.800
You're incredible.

00:54:25.800 --> 00:54:31.460
No street racer will challenge
 you to a downhill battle in Akina.

00:54:31.460 --> 00:54:32.920
I don't think so.

00:54:33.920 --> 00:54:38.710
There're plenty of good drivers in
 Gunma, because its skill level is high.

00:54:38.710 --> 00:54:42.310
I don't think Takahashi Ryosuke
 of the Red Suns can remain quiet.

00:54:43.210 --> 00:54:44.800
Takahashi Ryosuke, huh ?

00:54:47.160 --> 00:54:50.000
Speaking of which, he's fast.

00:54:51.260 --> 00:54:56.200
When I was fighting the GT-R,
 a white RX7 was right on my tail.

00:54:57.500 --> 00:55:01.300
I was occupied chasing the GT-R at the time...

00:55:01.300 --> 00:55:04.250
{atode}...but looking back on it, he concerns me.

00:55:04.250 --> 00:55:11.050
{ore}I know for sure. He's really fast,
 faster than anyone we've ever seen.

00:55:11.750 --> 00:55:14.590
I see. Probably so.

00:55:14.590 --> 00:55:21.570
Hey, Takumi, what would you do if 
a great racer like him challenged you ?

00:55:22.500 --> 00:55:25.550
You won't accept, right ?

00:55:27.450 --> 00:55:30.600
If that happens...

00:55:31.650 --> 00:55:34.070
...I'll take a shot.

00:55:41.120 --> 00:55:42.620
I finally found you !

00:55:44.110 --> 00:55:45.200
Mogi...?

00:55:45.200 --> 00:55:46.600
Why are you here ?

00:55:47.100 --> 00:55:55.430
You only mentioned "gas station," so I've been looking for your work place for a long time.

00:55:55.430 --> 00:55:56.200
Why ?

00:55:56.820 --> 00:56:00.400
Because I wanted to see you at work.

00:56:01.890 --> 00:56:04.560
Itsuki, who is she ?

00:56:04.560 --> 00:56:07.000
A classmate, but um...

00:56:07.550 --> 00:56:09.570
Your bellybutton's showing.

00:56:10.350 --> 00:56:13.000
That's fine.
 This's how it's supposed to look.

00:56:14.090 --> 00:56:18.150
Hello. I have a flower delivery,
 and need your signature.

00:56:18.650 --> 00:56:23.150
It's addressed to Mr. Panda Trueno.

00:56:23.150 --> 00:56:25.040
Panda Trueno...?

00:56:25.040 --> 00:56:27.660
Takumi, that must be you.

00:56:27.660 --> 00:56:28.580
Me ?

00:56:29.300 --> 00:56:32.000
A bouquet for Takumi ?

00:56:33.000 --> 00:56:34.450
From who ?

00:56:35.350 --> 00:56:36.900
There. A letter.

00:56:37.550 --> 00:56:39.250
Open it quickly.

00:56:41.000 --> 00:56:43.000
From who ? Who is it ?

00:56:59.700 --> 00:57:01.360
So who sent it ?

00:57:11.900 --> 00:57:15.200
August 27th at 10PM

00:57:11.900 --> 00:57:15.200
 Will be waiting at the peak of Mt. Akina

00:57:11.900 --> 00:57:15.200
Takahashi Ryosuke

00:57:27.400 --> 00:57:33.250
{mimi wo fusaidemo kikoeru kodou}Even when my ears are covered, I hear the heartbeat getting...

